## Resolved mutable: m-player-fps-lod-demotion

REFUTED as the cause. browser-131: the player pool entity (id 1) has trackedMeshes:0 and lastScreenPx:null -- the player VRM is NOT managed by the pool's trackedMesh LOD system (it renders via the VRM multi-driver, driveVrm:false). So the FPS-driven _lodDistanceScale collapse (0.40 live) demotes pool LODs but does NOT touch the player. The player has 8362 tris (full mesh present) but shows 'few moving verts' -> NOT a LOD demotion. This is a SKINNING/SKELETON bug: the full mesh exists but most bones' skin matrices are wrong (identity/zero), so most verts collapse to bind pose / origin while only a few correctly-bound bones animate ('few moving verts' + 'snap to 0'). Cause is the VRM multi-driver per-instance skeleton rebind in streaming-gltf (combineSkeletons/removeUnnecessaryVertices + the N-independent-skeleton clone), not LOD.